P NAV ============================================ --> <nav class="topnav"> <div class="topnav-inner"> <div class="topnav-brand"><strong>bea</strong> · three directions</div> <div class="topnav-nav"> <a href="#intro">Intro</a> <a href="#a">A · Long View</a> <a href="#b">B · Specialist</a> <a href="#c">C · Luminescence</a> <a href="#decide">Decide</a> </div> </div> </nav> <!-- ============================================ INTRO ============================================ --> <section id="intro" class="intro"> <div class="intro-inner"> <div class="intro-eyebrow">Bea Skin Care · Creative Directions · April 2026</div> <h1 class="intro-title">Three ways to<br><em>become</em> Bea.</h1> <p class="intro-lead">The brand story that came out of Discovery has three layers: a position, a proof, and a flagship. Each of them is strong enough to lead the whole visual system. What follows are three fully-built directions, each led by a different layer.</p>
<div class="intro-story">
  <div class="intro-story-label">The story,<br>as it stands</div>
  <dl class="intro-story-layers">
    <div class="intro-story-layer">
      <dt>Position</dt>
      <dd>Skin health for the long term.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-story-layer">
      <dt>Proof</dt>
      <dd>Formulated and tested in the clinic.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-story-layer">
      <dt>Flagship</dt>
      <dd>Luminescence, the range that started it all.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</div>

<p style="font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--ink-mute); max-width: 64ch; margin-bottom: 2rem; font-style: normal; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; background: rgba(168,163,152,0.08); border-left: 2px solid var(--stone);"><strong style="color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500;">A note on the proof layer.</strong> Bianca's own articulation references the clinic. Bea Skin Care Limited is a separate company from Bianca's clinical practice, so the language we use commercially needs to reflect that. Direction B translates the proof layer into <em>"formulated by a clinical specialist"</em> rather than <em>"tested in the clinic"</em> — keeping the credibility Bianca built up over fifteen years of practice, without conflating Bea with a separate business or implying formal clinical trials that did not take place.</p>

<p>All three directions keep the honeycomb, because it's the most distinctive thing Bea owns. Beyond that, they go in three different visual directions, with three different typographic systems, three different palettes, and three different photography briefs. They are not three shades of the same idea. They are three brands that Bea could credibly become.</p>

<div class="intro-directions">
  <a href="#a" class="intro-direction">
    <div class="intro-direction-tag">Direction A · Position-led</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-title">The Long View</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-lead">Skin as biology. Editorial science journal. Typography does the talking. Philosophical, quiet, durable.</div>
  </a>
  <a href="#b" class="intro-direction">
    <div class="intro-direction-tag">Direction B · Proof-led</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-title">The Specialist</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-lead">Bianca as the trained eye behind every formulation. Practitioner's notebook. Considered evidence. Clinical credibility without overclaim.</div>
  </a>
  <a href="#c" class="intro-direction">
    <div class="intro-direction-tag">Direction C · Flagship-led</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-title">Luminescence</div>
    <div class="intro-direction-lead">Bianca's personal journey. The honeycomb amplified. Warm, confident, commercial. The range that started it, leading the whole brand.</div>
  </a>
</div>

