</div> </section> <!-- ============================================ DIRECTION A — THE LONG VIEW ============================================ --> <section id="a" class="direction a"> <div class="direction-label"> <div class="direction-label-tag">Direction A</div> </div> <div class="a-hero"> <div class="a-hero-inner"> <div class="a-hero-text"> <div class="a-mark-tiny"> <svg viewBox="0 0 280 320"><use href="#honeycomb-outline"/></svg> <span class="a-mark-tiny-text">bea · the long view</span> </div> <h2 class="a-essence">Skin works<br>on a <em>longer</em><br>timescale<br>than we do.</h2> <p class="a-essence-sub">A brand built around what skin needs to keep doing for the rest of a lifetime. Patient formulations. Quiet products. The full benefit measured in years, not weeks.</p> </div> <div class="a-hero-still"> <div class="a-still-caption">No. 01 · Brightening Serum</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="a-section"> <div class="a-section-inner"> <div class="a-section-num">01 · The story it tells</div> <h3 class="a-section-title">The thinking,<br>not just the <em>products</em>.</h3> <p class="a-body">This direction takes the answer Bianca gave to question 28 of the brand discovery and makes it the entire brand. Not "brightening for radiant skin", but skincare formulated with what skin will be doing in ten years in mind. The conversation stops being about the next tube and becomes about what you are asking your skin to keep doing for the rest of your life.</p> <p class="a-body">Visually it borrows from the longevity-skincare tradition rather than the editorial-magazine tradition. Generous space. Almost no colour. Photography that is more still life than product shot. Type that breathes. The products earn their place by belonging to a serious conversation, not by shouting.</p>
  <div class="a-pull">
    The intention behind the products is not just short-term cosmetic improvement, but supporting the skin's ability to repair, regenerate and remain healthy over time.
    <span class="a-pull-attr">Bianca · Brand Discovery, Q28</span>
  </div>
</div>
</div> <div class="a-section"> <div class="a-section-inner"> <div class="a-section-num">02 · The mark</div> <h3 class="a-section-title">Honeycomb in <em>outline</em>.<br>Wordmark in serif.<br>Almost a watermark.</h3> <p class="a-body">The honeycomb is drawn fine, in outline, almost as if pressed into paper. Smaller than usual, used as a signature rather than a sign. The wordmark sits in Cormorant Garamond, a serif that carries quietness rather than weight. The whole mark is restrained on purpose: it is meant to be present without announcing itself.</p>
  <div class="a-wordmark-demo">
    <div class="a-wordmark">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 280 320"><use href="#honeycomb-outline"/></svg>
      <div class="a-wordmark-text">bea</div>
