</div>
</div> <div class="a-section"> <div class="a-section-inner"> <div class="a-section-num">06 · A homepage moment</div> <h3 class="a-section-title">The site reads<br>like a <em>chapter</em>,<br>not a catalogue.</h3>
  <div class="a-homepage-demo">
    <div class="a-homepage-eyebrow">No. 01 · On Pigmentation</div>
    <h4 class="a-homepage-hero">Skin keeps a <em>record</em> of everything it has done.</h4>
    <p class="a-homepage-body">Pigmentation is skin keeping a record of sunlight, inflammation and time. The Luminescence range does not erase the record. It helps skin rewrite the chapters you no longer want it to repeat.</p>
    <a href="#" class="a-link">Read the range →</a>
  </div>
</div>
</div> <div class="a-section"> <div class="a-section-inner"> <div class="a-section-num">07 · A product in this world</div> <h3 class="a-section-title">The card is <em>quiet</em>.<br>The name does the work.</h3>
  <div class="a-product-card">
    <div class="a-product-image"></div>
    <div class="a-product-meta">
      <div class="a-product-eyebrow">No. 01 · Luminescence</div>
      <div class="a-product-name">The Brightening <em>Serum</em></div>
      <div class="a-product-desc">A daily serum for uneven tone, hyperpigmentation and the skin's own brightness over time.</div>
      <div class="a-product-price">£55 · 30ml</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="a-tradeoff">
    <div>
      <h4>What this direction is best at</h4>
      <p>Authenticity to Bianca's own language. International fit, because a longevity philosophy translates across markets without needing to be rewritten for each one. Durability — it ages well because it is not chasing a trend. A genuinely distinctive position in a category dominated by clinical-functional and clean-beauty registers.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4>What it trades off</h4>
      <p>Commercial clarity on the homepage. Philosophy does not sell a cleanser as directly as a concern does. Requires confidence from Bianca that the brand's point of view is enough on its own, and patience with conversion rates in the first six months as the audience adjusts.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</div> </section> <!-- ============================================ DIRECTION B — THE CLINIC ============================================ --> <section id="b" class="direction b"> <div class="direction-label"> <div class="direction-label-tag">Direction B</div> </div> <div class="b-hero"> <div class="b-hero-inner"> <div class="b-hero-left"> <div class="b-clinical-code"> <span>Formulator's notes</span> <span>Ref 2017/001</span> <span>London</span> </div> <h2 class="b-essence">Made by someone<br>who has spent<br><strong>fifteen years</strong><br>looking at skin.</h2> <p class="b-essence-sub">A brand built around the formulator. Bianca trained as an aesthetic specialist before Bea existed. Every product carries the same eye, the same standard, the same patience that her practice does.</p> </div> <div class="b-hero-right"> <div class="b-specimen-card"> <div class="b-specimen-header"> <span>Formulation log</span> <span>23.04.2022</span> </div> <div class="b-specimen-title">Brightening Serum v4.1</div> <div class="b-specimen-meta">15% L-AA · 1% Tocopherol · pH 3.2 · 18 months in development</div> </div> <div class="b-specimen-card"> <div class="b-specimen-header"> <span>Released</span> <span>02.09.2023</span> </div> <div class="b-specimen-title">Kojic Acid Radiance Bar</div> <div class="b-specimen-meta">2% Kojic · Glycerin base · Body · Assessed against four predecessor formulations</div> </div> <div class="b-specimen-card"> <div class="b-specimen-header"> <span>In development</span> <span>Current</span> </div> <div class="b-specimen-title">Peptide Booster v2</div> <div class="b-specimen-meta">Matrixyl 3000 · Copper peptides · Reformulation underway</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">01 · Story</div> <div class="b-section-name">The formulator is the brand.</div> <div class="b-section-desc">What it looks like when the trained eye behind the products is the thing the brand stands on.</div> </div> <div> <p class="b-section-body">This direction answers a single question: why should the customer believe Bea? By making the formulator visible. The years of practice. The professional standard the products are held to. The reformulations. The slow build of a range that has been in development since 2017.</p> <p class="b-section-body">The Discovery work flagged that very few brands at this tier have a working aesthetic specialist behind every formulation. This direction cashes in on that without overclaiming. Bea does not run trials. Bea does not make medical claims. What Bea does have is fifteen years of professional eye, and that is the thing the brand puts forward.</p>
    <div class="b-notebook">
      <div class="b-notebook-header">
        <span class="b-notebook-title">From the formulator's notes</span>
        <span class="b-notebook-date">12.11.2022</span>
      </div>
      <div class="b-notebook-body">
        Reformulated the Brightening Serum a fourth time this morning. Lowered the vitamin C to 15% after the previous concentration sat less comfortably with sensitive skin. Added a second tocopherol for stability. Back into the fridge for three weeks. I will not move it any further toward release until I am sure it earns its place in the range.
      </div>
      <div class="b-notebook-sig">— BES, formulator</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">02 · The mark</div> <div class="b-section-name">Honeycomb.<br>Clean sans.<br>Provenance line.</div> </div> <div> <div class="b-wordmark-demo"> <div class="b-wordmark"> <svg class="b-wordmark-hex" viewBox="0 0 280 320"><use href="#honeycomb-solid"/></svg> <div class="b-wordmark-text">bea</div> <div class="b-wordmark-ref">Formulated in London · Est. 2017</div> </div> </div> <p class="b-section-body">The honeycomb is drawn solid in the deep blue of the accent palette. The wordmark is set tight and heavy, closer to a professional mark than a beauty mark. The provenance line under the wordmark says only what is true: where the product is formulated, and when the brand began.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">03 · Palette</div> <div class="b-section-name">White. Deep blue. Graphite.</div> </div> <div> <p class="b-section-body">A practitioner palette without being cold. White does most of the work. A single deep blue replaces the current peach accent, reading as professional rather than promotional. Graphite for type. The colour system carries the same disciplined feel as the formulator's eye.</p>
