</div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">04 · Typography</div> <div class="b-section-name">Inter Tight.<br>Plex Serif for notes.<br>Plex Mono for specifications.</div> </div> <div> <div class="b-type-row"> <div class="b-type-label">Display · Inter Tight 600</div> <div class="b-type-1">Brightening Serum</div> </div> <div class="b-type-row"> <div class="b-type-label">Heading · Inter Tight 500</div> <div class="b-type-2">Eighteen months in development. Four reformulations. One that finally earned the name.</div> </div> <div class="b-type-row"> <div class="b-type-label">Notes · Plex Serif italic</div> <div class="b-type-3">The brightening work is slow. The full benefit shows up at twelve weeks, not at four. Patience is part of the formulation.</div> </div> <div class="b-type-row"> <div class="b-type-label">Spec · Plex Mono</div> <div class="b-type-4">15% L-AA · 1% TOCOPHEROL · pH 3.2 · 30ML</div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">05 · Photography</div> <div class="b-section-name">Considered. Hands at work.</div> </div> <div> <p class="b-section-body">Documentary register, but careful about what is shown. Bianca's hands. Formulation in progress. A studio bench, not a treatment room. The photography reads as an extended commission about a working formulator, not a marketing shoot dressed up as one.</p>
    <div class="b-photo b-photo-clinic">
      <div class="b-photo-meta">
        <span>Ref. 2024/04/12</span>
        <span>Formulation studio</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</div> <div class="b-section"> <div class="b-section-inner"> <div class="b-section-label"> <div class="b-section-code">06 · A product in this world</div> <div class="b-section-name">Specification card. Not promotion.</div> </div> <div> <div class="b-product-spec"> <div class="b-product-header"> <span class="b-product-code">SPEC · LUM-S-015</span> <span class="b-product-status">● Released</span> </div> <div class="b-product-body"> <div class="b-product-name">Brightening Serum</div> <div class="b-product-sub">"Eighteen months in development. The fourth version was the one I would put my name to."</div> <div class="b-product-specs"> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>Formulated</span><span>Jan 2022</span></div> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>Released</span><span>Sep 2023</span></div> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>Active</span><span>L-AA 15%</span></div> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>pH</span><span>3.2</span></div> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>Versions</span><span>4</span></div> <div class="b-product-spec-row"><span>Volume</span><span>30ml</span></div> </div> </div> <div class="b-product-footer"> <span class="b-product-price">£55.00</span> <button class="b-btn">Add to bag</button> </div> </div>
    <div class="b-tradeoff">
      <div>
        <h4>What this direction is best at</h4>
        <p>Defensibility. Bianca's professional credentials are an asset almost no other brand at this tier can claim. International fit, because professional credibility translates cleanly. Authenticity to what Bianca actually does as a formulator, without conflating Bea with the separate clinical practice.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h4>What it trades off</h4>
        <p>Warmth. The brand can read as cold if the photography and copy do not bring Bianca forward as a person. Requires Bianca to be visible as the formulator throughout, which is a long-term commitment. Care needed with claims language: "formulated by", "developed by", "made by" all work; "tested on", "trialled on", "clinically proven" do not.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</div> </section> <!-- ============================================ DIRECTION C — LUMINESCENCE LEGACY ============================================ --> <section id="c" class="direction c"> <div class="direction-label"> <div class="direction-label-tag">Direction C</div> </div> <div class="c-hero"> <div class="c-hero-inner"> <div class="c-hero-grid"> <div> <div class="c-eyebrow">Luminescence · A Legacy</div> <h2 class="c-essence">The range<br>that <em>started</em><br>it all.</h2> <p class="c-essence-sub">This is the brand built around Bianca's own story. Her own journey with hyperpigmentation, the range she formulated to answer it, and the honeycomb that has been her mark from the beginning.</p> </div> <div class="c-hero-art"> <svg class="c-big-honeycomb" viewBox="0 0 280 320"><use href="#honeycomb-solid"/></svg> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="c-section"> <div class="c-section-inner"> <div class="c-section-head"> <div class="c-section-num">01 · Story</div> <h3 class="c-section-title">A founder with <em>a face</em>,<br>and a range that means something.</h3> </div> <p class="c-body">Direction C leads with Luminescence because it is both the commercial engine and the personal story. Bianca's own experience with hyperpigmentation is the reason the range exists. The brand stops being abstract and becomes a founder, a journey, and a range that answers it.</p> <p class="c-body">The visual language is warmer than either of the other two directions. Peach, amber and cream. The honeycomb is amplified, set large, used as decoration as well as mark. The photography shows real skin, diverse skin, and Bianca's skin specifically — because the brand has a face, and that face is one of the reasons to buy it.</p>
  <div class="c-founder-block">
