<div class="decide-next">
  <h3>Where I'd lean, and why.</h3>
  <p>Direction B (the Specialist) scores strongest on four of five criteria and is the only one that turns Bianca's years of professional training into a brand asset without conflating Bea with the separate clinical business. It gives Bianca the most honest version of the brand, because it is built on what she actually does as a formulator. The risk it carries is warmth, and that risk is addressable: let the founder's voice sit inside the specialist frame rather than outside it. That might mean borrowing the founder-led warmth of Direction C and embedding it in the considered register of Direction B. A hybrid is on the table. The next conversation is which one Bianca feels is closest to her, and where she wants to stretch.</p>
